Z||000003||WisconsinGT||12-26-1999||01:37 AM||||Sorry to hear that Fieroshop. I guess we got the same gift this year. I thank god for giving me the wisdom to not have kids with my soon to be ex-wife. Hope all goes well for you.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||12-26-1999||08:35 AM||||It really sucks to get divorced (been there done that), especially around the holidays. It can be very depressing. It sure tore me up for a couple years. Maybe all us spurn Fiero Forum members can meet someday for a cruise, then afterwards drink beer, talk Fieros, and verbally bash ex-spouses.<P>Seems like nowadays if the road gets a little rough, instead of slowing down some then swerving to avoid the biggest potholes and riding out the smaller bumps, it's easier to just turn down another street that is smoother (at least for a little while anyway).||||reg||1
Z||000005||TOM||12-26-1999||01:58 PM||||Sorry to hear of the loss. But it sounds like it is for the better. It is still rough to go through as breakup. Best of luck. Is the new shop locale in LA? ||||reg||1
